    "created_at": "2017-11-17T15:44:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-17T15:44:14Z",
    "body": "No, in general the .click() method is not meant to trigger user interfaces, especially in cases where it's a UI/implementation detail that clicking triggers an input at all. For example, you could implement a browser that shows the picker on hover, or on focus, and for those this behavior would make no sense. So its inclusion in those mobile browsers is an interoperability hazard, as you've already found by comparing them to desktop browsers. So that's why this is definitely a browser bug.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
