    "updated_at": "2018-03-07T15:55:45Z",
    "body": "I have tested https://output.jsbin.com/sonopow/quiet on Edge 16 and Safari TP.\r\n\r\nIn Edge it doesn't cause the date picker to be shown, and in Safari it seems like `<input type=date>` isn't supported, and https://caniuse.com/#feat=input-datetime agrees, so obviously calling `click()` doesn't do anything.\r\n\r\nIn other words, Firefox is the outlier. We should file a Firefox bug and close this issue, I think. Anything I've overlooked?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
