    "updated_at": "2018-03-14T16:23:48Z",
    "body": "Oh, I didn't pay attention to the platform differences. In the absence of specified \"activation behavior\" the right-per-spec thing is that `click()` does nothing. To add activation behavior seems odd, because at least in Chrome pressing space and enter doesn't do the same thing as clicking. If we could get away with it, just not having activation behavior seems better to me.",
